                                           None   \n","3                                               None   \n","4  Ar laiku paliek skaidrāk, jo uzņēmies vairāk a...   \n","\n","                        Novērtējums_Komentāri  \\\n","0                                        None   \n","1                                        None   \n","2  Minētie novērtējumi ir par to, ko vēlētos.   \n","3                                        None   \n","4   Iespēja dabūt apmaksātus kursus, mācības.   \n","\n","  Priekšlikumi_tiešajam_vadītājam_Komentāri Saziņa_Komentāri  \\\n","0                                      None             None   \n","1                                      None             None   \n","2                                      None             None   \n","3                                      None             None   \n","4                                      None          Epasts.   \n","\n","                                    Stress_Komentāri  \\\n","0                                               None   \n","1                                               None   \n","2  Darbu apjoms - pēc klusākām dienām nāk pārpild...   \n","3                                               None   \n","4                                               None   \n","\n","                 Tiešā_vadītāja_kompetence_Komentāri  \\\n","0                                               None   \n","1                                               None   \n","2                                               None   \n","3                                               None   \n","4  Dažreiz liekas ke ne, bet tas laikam man dēļ p...   \n","\n","                                         Vēlme_darīt  \\\n","0              Cītīgi pildīt savus darba pienākumus.   \n","1                            Apmeklēt jaunus kursus.   \n","2                      Mācīties un uzņemties vairāk.   \n","3  Gatavs palīdzēt veidot un piedalīties procesos...   \n","4  Jau daru, mācos kursos un naktis par IT.\\r\\nLa...   \n","\n","  Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Komentāri Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs_Komentāri  \n","0                              None                                     None  \n","1                              None                                     None  \n","2                              None                                     None  \n","3                              None                                     None  \n","4                              None                                     None  \n","                           Apmācības_vajadzības_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                                   4   \n","unique                                                  4   \n","top     Vēlētos apgūt darba optimizāciju, un izprast v...   \n","freq                                                    1   \n","\n","                                   Darba_slodze_komentārs  \\\n","count                                                  10   \n","unique                                                 10   \n","top     Vairāk ne, jo vajag iet ārpus sava darba apjom...   \n","freq                                                    1   \n","\n","                                   Darba_laiks__komentāri Ieteikumi  \\\n","count                                                   5        34   \n","unique                                                  5        34   \n","top     Un ja un ne, dažreiz var aiziet mājas laikus, ...      Nav.   \n","freq                                                    1         1   \n","\n","       Informācija_no_tiešā_vadītāja_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                        5   \n","unique                                       5   \n","top                           Bez komentāriem.   \n","freq                                         1   \n","\n","       Informācija_no_uzņēmuma_vadības_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                          5   \n","unique                                         5   \n","top                                       90% jā   \n","freq                                           1   \n","\n","                 Izpratne_par_darba_pienākumiem_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                                   6   \n","unique                                                  6   \n","top     Nē, līdz šim nav līdz galam skaidrs kas ir man...   \n","freq                                                    1   \n","\n","                       Nepieciešamā_informācija_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                                   7   \n","unique                                                  7   \n","top     Ar laiku paliek skaidrāk, jo uzņēmies vairāk a...   \n","freq                                                    1   \n","\n","                             Novērtējums_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                            4   \n","unique                                           4   \n","top     Minētie novērtējumi ir par to, ko vēlētos.   \n","freq                                             1   \n","\n","        Priekšlikumi_tiešajam_vadītājam_Komentāri Saziņa_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                           3                5   \n","unique                                          3                5   \n","top     Uzklausa, dažreiz ņem vērā, ar ko pietiek          Epasts.   \n","freq                                            1                1   \n","\n","                                         Stress_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                                   8   \n","unique                                                  8   \n","top     Darbu apjoms - pēc klusākām dienām nāk pārpild...   \n","freq                                                    1   \n","\n","                      Tiešā_vadītāja_kompetence_Komentāri Vēlme_darīt  \\\n","count                                                   5          54   \n","unique                                                  5          50   \n","top     Dažreiz liekas ke ne, bet tas laikam man dēļ p...           -   \n","freq                                                    1           3   \n","\n","       Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Komentāri  \\\n","count                                  6   \n","unique                                 6   \n","top                             Jā un Nē   \n","freq                                   1   \n","\n","       Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs_Komentāri  \n","count                                         4  \n","unique                                        4  \n","top                    Nevar ieklikšķināt bet 9  \n","freq                                          1  \n","count      54.000000\n","mean      342.962963\n","std       401.233286\n","min        73.000000\n","25%        97.250000\n","50%       176.500000\n","75%       448.250000\n","max      2271.000000\n","Name: comment_length, dtype: float64\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# prompt: \tA Well-being-to-Engagement (WER) Ratio was calculated by dividing self-reported well-being scores by the binary value of whether an employee would recommend the organization.\n","# Key Metric – Well-being-to-Engagement Ratio (WER)\n","# WER=((Avarage Well-being Score)/(Avarage Enagagement Score)) \t\t\t(5.)\n","# Self-reported satisfaction (Q14)\n","# Engagement Score =\n","# +1 for willingness to recommend (Q15)\n","# +1 for suggesting improvements (Q16)\n","# +1 for willingness to act (Q17)\n","# Use data from: /content/processed_features_X.parquet and /content/processed_target_y.csv\n","\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","# Load the processed data\n","X = pd.read_parquet('/content/processed_features_X.parquet')\n","y = pd.read_csv('/content/processed_target_y.csv')\n","\n","# Ensure 'Engagement Score' is a binary column (1 for recommends, 0 otherwise)\n","# Assuming the target 'y' represents the willingness to recommend (Q15) and it's already binary (0 or 1)\n","# If 'y' is not binary, you might need to convert it based on the definition of Q15\n","# For example, if Q15 has values like 'Yes'/'No', you would map them to 1/0\n","# Assuming y is already the binary willingness to recommend (Q15)\n","\n","# Assuming X contains the 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' column (Well-being Score Q14)\n","# Ensure 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' exists in X and is numeric\n","if 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' not in X.columns:\n","    raise ValueError(\"Column 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' (Well-being Score) not found in processed_features_X.parquet\")\n","\n","# Calculate average well-being score for employees who would recommend (Engagement Score = 1)\n","# and for those who would not recommend (Engagement Score = 0)\n","# We need to align X and y based on their indices to ensure we are comparing the correct rows\n","# Assuming X and y have the same index and represent the same respondents\n","data = pd.concat([X, y], axis=1)\n","\n","# Rename the target column for clarity if it's not already named meaningfully\n","# Assuming the target column in y is the first column if it's not named\n","if y.columns[0] not in data.columns:\n","    data = pd.concat([X, y.rename(columns={y.columns[0]: 'Willingness_to_Recommend'})], axis=1)\n","    engagement_col_name = 'Willingness_to_Recommend'\n","else:\n","    # Assuming the relevant engagement column is already in y\n","    # You need to identify the correct column name for the binary willingness to recommend (Q15)\n","    # Let's assume it's named 'Q15_recommend' based on the description, replace with the actual name\n","    # Or if 'y' itself is the binary recommendation score:\n","    if y.columns[0] == 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs':\n","         raise ValueError(\"Target column in y seems to be Well-being Score, not Engagement Score (Willingness to Recommend). Please load the correct target.\")\n","    engagement_col_name = y.columns[0] # Assuming the first column of y is the engagement score (Q15)\n","\n","\n","if engagement_col_name not in data.columns:\n","     raise ValueError(f\"Engagement column '{engagement_col_name}' (Willingness to Recommend Q15) not found.\")\n","\n","# Ensure engagement column is treated as boolean or integer 0/1\n","data[engagement_col_name] = data[engagement_col_name].astype(int)\n","\n","# Ensure Well-being score is numeric\n","data['Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'] = pd.to_numeric(data['Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'], errors='coerce')\n","\n","# Drop rows where Well-being or Engagement is missing\n","data.dropna(subset=['Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs', engagement_col_name], inplace=True)\n","\n","# Calculate average well-being score for each engagement group\n","average_wellbeing_by_engagement = data.groupby(engagement_col_name)['Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'].mean()\n","\n","# Get the average well-being score for those who recommend (Engagement Score = 1)\n","average_wellbeing_recommended = average_wellbeing_by_engagement.get(1, 0) # Default to 0 if no recommenders\n","\n","# The formula defines WER as (Average Well-being Score) / (Average Engagement Score)\n","# The \"Average Engagement Score\" in this context refers to the *average of the binary willingness to recommend score*\n","# This is equivalent to the proportion of employees who recommend.\n","average_engagement_score = data[engagement_col_name].mean()\n","\n","# Calculate the Well-being-to-Engagement Ratio (WER)\n","if average_engagement_score > 0:\n","    wer_ratio = average_wellbeing_recommended / average_engagement_score\n","else:\n","    wer_ratio = np.nan # Avoid division by zero if no one recommends\n","\n","print(f\"Average Well-being Score for those who recommend (Engagement = 1): {average_wellbeing_recommended:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Average Engagement Score (Proportion who recommend): {average_engagement_score:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Well-being-to-Engagement (WER) Ratio: {wer_ratio:.2f}\")\n","\n","# Note: The definition provided seems to calculate the ratio based on the *average well-being score of recommenders*\n","# divided by the *average engagement score* (which is the proportion of recommenders).\n","# If the intention was to divide the *overall* average well-being by the overall average engagement,\n","# the calculation would be:\n","# overall_average_wellbeing = data['Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'].mean()\n","# overall_wer_ratio = overall_average_wellbeing / average_engagement_score if average_engagement_score > 0 else np.nan\n","# print(f\"Overall Average Well-being Score: {overall_average_wellbeing:.2f}\")\n","# print(f\"Overall WER Ratio: {overall_wer_ratio:.2f}\")\n","\n","# Based on the description \"dividing self-reported well-being scores by the binary value of whether an employee would recommend the organization\",\n","# and the formula provided, it is more likely intended to calculate the average well-being for the recommending group\n","# and divide it by the proportion of recommending employees (the average of the binary engagement).\n","# The code implements this interpretation."],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":211},"id":"oBtHVEDF7zpw","executionInfo":{"status":"error","timestamp":1748314457467,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":154,"user":{"displayName":"Vija Niedre","userId":"16452881736730193225"}},"outputId":"fff56f3b-4a96-4b24-d89a-b8170e0a1981"},"execution_count":37,"outputs":[{"output_type":"error","ename":"ValueError","evalue":"Column 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' (Well-being Score) not found in processed_features_X.parquet","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mValueError\u001b[0m                                Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m<ipython-input-37-f0832d14e645>\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     24\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# Ensure 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' exists in X and is numeric\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     25\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mif\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mnot\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32min\u001b[0m \u001b[0mX\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mcolumns\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m---> 26\u001b[0;31m     \u001b[0;32mraise\u001b[0m \u001b[0mValueError\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\"Column 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' (Well-being Score) not found in processed_features_X.parquet\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m     27\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     28\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# Calculate average well-being score for employees who would recommend (Engagement Score = 1)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;31mValueError\u001b[0m: Column 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs' (Well-being Score) not found in processed_features_X.parquet"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# Load the processed data\n","# Assuming these files contain the necessary data after prior processing\n","X = pd.read_parquet('/content/processed_features_X.parquet')\n","y = pd.read_csv('/content/processed_target_y.csv')\n","\n","# Assume y contains the Well-being Score (Q14) and X contains features, including the binary Engagement Score components (Q15, Q16, Q17)\n","\n","# Ensure y has a meaningful column name for the Well-being Score\n","wellbeing_col_name = 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'\n","# Assuming y is a single column DataFrame and its content is the wellbeing score\n","# If y has a header row, this might need adjustment.\n","# A safer approach might be to load y and then explicitly rename the column.\n","y.columns = [wellbeing_col_name]\n","\n","# Identify the columns in X that represent the binary components of the Engagement Score (Q15, Q16, Q17)\n","# You need to replace these placeholder names with the actual column names in your processed X DataFrame.\n","# These should be binary (0 or 1) columns.\n","# Based on your request:\n","# Q15 (Willingness to recommend): 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju' binary -> 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary' (or similar name after processing)\n","# Q16 (Suggesting improvements): 'Ieteikumi' (sentiment results, positive=1, negative=0) -> 'Ieteikumi_Sentiment_Binary' (or similar)\n","# Q17 (Willingness to act): 'Vēlme_darīt' (sentiment results, positive=1, negative=0) -> 'Vēlme_darīt_Sentiment_Binary' (or similar)\n","\n","# **CRITICAL: Replace these with the actual column names in your X DataFrame**\n","q15_col_name = 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary' # Placeholder - Replace with actual name"],"metadata":{"id":"n16bmAq-wWGk","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1748316050201,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":80,"user":{"displayName":"Vija Niedre","userId":"16452881736730193225"}}},"execution_count":40,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","# Load the processed data\n","X = pd.read_parquet('/content/processed_features_X.parquet')\n","y = pd.read_csv('/content/processed_target_y.csv')\n","\n","# Assume y contains the Well-being Score (Q14) and X contains features, including the binary Engagement Score (Q15)\n","\n","# Ensure y has a meaningful column name for the Well-being Score\n","wellbeing_col_name = 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'\n","# Assuming y is a single column DataFrame and its content is the wellbeing score\n","y.columns = [wellbeing_col_name]\n","\n","# Identify the column in X that represents the binary Willingness to Recommend (Engagement Score Q15)\n","# You need to replace 'ACTUAL_Q15_BINARY_COLUMN_NAME_IN_X' with the correct column name.\n","# This could be the original column name if it wasn't one-hot encoded,\n","# or a one-hot encoded column representing the positive recommendation.\n","engagement_col_name = 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary' # <-- REPLACE with the actual column name in X for binary Q15\n","\n","if engagement_col_name not in X.columns:\n","     # If the binary Q15 column is not directly in X with a simple name,\n","     # you might need to search for it or derive it from the one-hot encoded columns.\n","     # For example, if 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju' was one-hot encoded, look for columns\n","     # starting with 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_'.\n","     potential_q15_cols = [col for col in X.columns if col.startswith('Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_')]\n","     if potential_q15_cols:\n","         print(f\"Found potential Q15 columns in X: {potential_q15_cols}\")\n","         # You need to decide which of these columns represents the binary 'recommend' state (1).\n","         # Let's assume for demonstration it's the first one found, but VERIFY this.\n","         engagement_col_name = potential_q15_cols[0]\n","         print(f\"Using '{engagement_col_name}' as the engagement column.\")\n","     else:\n","         raise ValueError(f\"Engagement column '{engagement_col_name}' (Willingness to Recommend Q15) not found in X, and no potential Q15 columns found.\")\n","\n","\n","# Combine X and y for easier calculation, aligning by index\n","# Ensure X and y have the same index\n","if not X.index.equals(y.index):\n","    # If indices don't match, you need to find a way to align them,\n","    # perhaps using an Employee ID column if available and common to both.\n","    # For now, assuming they are aligned.\n","    print(\"Warning: X and y indices do not match. Proceeding, but results may be incorrect if data is not aligned.\")\n","\n","data = pd.concat([X, y], axis=1)\n","\n","# Ensure engagement column is treated as integer 0/1 and well-being is numeric\n","data[engagement_col_name] = data[engagement_col_name].astype(int)\n","data[wellbeing_col_name] = pd.to_numeric(data[wellbeing_col_name], errors='coerce')\n","\n","# Drop rows where Well-being or Engagement is missing\n","data.dropna(subset=[wellbeing_col_name, engagement_col_name], inplace=True)\n","\n","# Calculate average well-being score for employees who would recommend (Engagement Score = 1)\n","average_wellbeing_recommended = data[data[engagement_col_name] == 1][wellbeing_col_name].mean()\n","\n","# The formula defines WER as (Average Well-being Score) / (Average Engagement Score)\n","# The \"Average Engagement Score\" in this context refers to the *average of the binary willingness to recommend score*\n","# This is equivalent to the proportion of employees who recommend.\n","average_engagement_score = data[engagement_col_name].mean()\n","\n","# Calculate the Well-being-to-Engagement Ratio (WER)\n","if average_engagement_score > 0:\n","    wer_ratio = average_wellbeing_recommended / average_engagement_score\n","else:\n","    wer_ratio = np.nan # Avoid division by zero if no one recommends\n","\n","print(f\"Average Well-being Score for those who recommend (Engagement = 1): {average_wellbeing_recommended:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Average Engagement Score (Proportion who recommend): {average_engagement_score:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Well-being-to-Engagement (WER) Ratio: {wer_ratio:.2f}\")\n","\n","# Note: The definition provided seems to calculate the ratio based on the *average well-being score of recommenders*\n","# divided by the *average engagement score* (which is the proportion of recommenders).\n","# If the intention was to divide the *overall* average well-being by the overall average engagement,\n","# the calculation would be:\n","# overall_average_wellbeing = data[wellbeing_col_name].mean()\n","# overall_wer_ratio = overall_average_wellbeing / average_engagement_score if average_engagement_score > 0 else np.nan\n","# print(f\"Overall Average Well-being Score: {overall_average_wellbeing:.2f}\")\n","# print(f\"Overall WER Ratio: {overall_wer_ratio:.2f}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"tNKl0XemJocU","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1748316067844,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":77,"user":{"displayName":"Vija Niedre","userId":"16452881736730193225"}},"outputId":"30dffcfd-a5fe-4fc7-a22f-1fb50c5e9d1b"},"execution_count":41,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Found potential Q15 columns in X: ['Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Ieteiktu', 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Neieteiktu', 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Komentāri_sentiment']\n","Using 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Ieteiktu' as the engagement column.\n","Average Well-being Score for those who recommend (Engagement = 1): 0.72\n","Average Engagement Score (Proportion who recommend): 0.87\n","Well-being-to-Engagement (WER) Ratio: 0.83\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","# Load the processed data\n","X = pd.read_parquet('/content/processed_features_X.parquet')\n","y = pd.read_csv('/content/processed_target_y.csv')\n","\n","# Assume y contains the Well-being Score (Q14) and X contains features, including the binary Engagement Score components (Q15, Q16, Q17)\n","\n","# Ensure y has a meaningful column name for the Well-being Score\n","wellbeing_col_name = 'Vispārējās_labsajūtas_rādītājs'\n","# Assuming y is a single column DataFrame and its content is the wellbeing score\n","y.columns = [wellbeing_col_name]\n","\n","# Identify the columns in X that represent the binary components of the Engagement Score (Q15, Q16, Q17)\n","# You need to replace these placeholder names with the actual column names in your processed X DataFrame.\n","# These should be binary (0 or 1) columns.\n","q15_col_name = 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary' # Replace with actual Q15 binary column name\n","q16_col_name = 'Sugestions_for_Improvement_Binary' # Replace with actual Q16 binary column name\n","q17_col_name = 'Willingness_to_Act_Binary' # Replace with actual Q17 binary column name\n","\n","# --- Validation checks for existence of Q15, Q16, Q17 columns in X ---\n","required_engagement_cols = [q15_col_name, q16_col_name, q17_col_name]\n","missing_cols = [col for col in required_engagement_cols if col not in X.columns]\n","\n","if missing_cols:\n","    # If the exact binary column names are not found, try to locate them\n","    # This part is similar to the original code's attempt to find Q15,\n","    # but needs to be adapted for Q16 and Q17 as well.\n","    print(f\"Required engagement columns not found directly: {missing_cols}\")\n","    print(\"Attempting to find potential columns based on names...\")\n","\n","    found_cols = {}\n","    for req_col in missing_cols:\n","        # Example: look for columns starting with the base name before '_Binary'\n","        base_name = req_col.replace('_Binary', '')\n","        potential_cols = [col for col in X.columns if col.startswith(base_name)]\n","        if potential_cols:\n","            print(f\"Found potential columns for '{req_col}': {potential_cols}\")\n","            # You need to manually verify which of these is the correct binary column (0 or 1)\n","            # For demonstration, we'll assume the first found potential column is correct,\n","            # but this is a critical step to get right with your actual data.\n","            selected_col = potential_cols[0] # VERIFY THIS IS THE CORRECT BINARY COLUMN\n","            print(f\"Using '{selected_col}' for '{req_col}'.\")\n","            found_cols[req_col] = selected_col\n","        else:\n","             raise ValueError(f\"Engagement component column '{req_col}' not found in X, and no potential columns found.\")\n","\n","    # Update the column names to the found ones\n","    q15_col_name = found_cols.get(q15_col_name, q15_col_name)\n","    q16_col_name = found_cols.get(q16_col_name, q16_col_name)\n","    q17_col_name = found_cols.get(q17_col_name, q17_col_name)\n","\n","# After validation, the column names should be correct or an error was raised.\n","# Proceed assuming q15_col_name, q16_col_name, q17_col_name hold the correct binary column names.\n","\n","\n","# Combine X and y for easier calculation, aligning by index\n","# Ensure X and y have the same index\n","if not X.index.equals(y.index):\n","    # If indices don't match, you need to find a way to align them,\n","    # perhaps using an Employee ID column if available and common to both.\n","    # For now, assuming they are aligned.\n","    print(\"Warning: X and y indices do not match. Proceeding, but results may be incorrect if data is not aligned.\")\n","\n","data = pd.concat([X, y], axis=1)\n","\n","# Ensure wellbeing column is numeric\n","data[wellbeing_col_name] = pd.to_numeric(data[wellbeing_col_name], errors='coerce')\n","\n","# Calculate the combined Engagement Score\n","# Ensure the engagement component columns are treated as integer 0/1 before summing\n","data[q15_col_name] = data[q15_col_name].astype(int)\n","data[q16_col_name] = data[q16_col_name].astype(int)\n","data[q17_col_name] = data[q17_col_name].astype(int)\n","\n","data['Combined_Engagement_Score'] = data[q15_col_name] + data[q16_col_name] + data[q17_col_name]\n","\n","# Drop rows where Well-being or the required Engagement components are missing\n","data.dropna(subset=[wellbeing_col_name, q15_col_name, q16_col_name, q17_col_name], inplace=True)\n","\n","\n","# Calculate average well-being score for the entire dataset\n","overall_average_wellbeing = data[wellbeing_col_name].mean()\n","\n","# Calculate the overall average of the combined Engagement Score\n","overall_average_engagement_score = data['Combined_Engagement_Score'].mean()\n","\n","# Calculate the Well-being-to-Engagement Ratio (WER) using overall averages\n","if overall_average_engagement_score > 0:\n","    wer_ratio = overall_average_wellbeing / overall_average_engagement_score\n","else:\n","    wer_ratio = np.nan # Avoid division by zero if average engagement is zero\n","\n","print(f\"Overall Average Well-being Score: {overall_average_wellbeing:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Overall Average Combined Engagement Score: {overall_average_engagement_score:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Well-being-to-Engagement (WER) Ratio: {wer_ratio:.2f}\")\n","\n","# Optional: Print average well-being for each level of the combined engagement score\n","print(\"\\nAverage Well-being Score by Combined Engagement Score Level:\")\n","print(data.groupby('Combined_Engagement_Score')[wellbeing_col_name].mean().round(2))"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":280},"id":"6tITEXGutLC4","executionInfo":{"status":"error","timestamp":1748316204419,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":78,"user":{"displayName":"Vija Niedre","userId":"16452881736730193225"}},"outputId":"555dd4ab-816d-4431-e0c2-5c6085605d6d"},"execution_count":43,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Required engagement columns not found directly: ['Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary', 'Sugestions_for_Improvement_Binary', 'Willingness_to_Act_Binary']\n","Attempting to find potential columns based on names...\n","Found potential columns for 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary': ['Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Ieteiktu', 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Neieteiktu', 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Komentāri_sentiment']\n","Using 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Ieteiktu' for 'Vēlme_ieteikt_kompāniju_Binary'.\n"]},{"output_type":"error","ename":"ValueError","evalue":"Engagement component column 'Sugestions_for_Improvement_Binary' not found in X, and no potential columns found.","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mValueError\u001b[0m                                Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m<ipython-input-43-8b43f1f35f3e>\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     44\u001b[0m             \u001b[0mfound_cols\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m[\u001b[0m\u001b[0mreq_col\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m]\